  "preamble": "Assibilation of the palatalized stop [dʲ] to the alveolar affricate [dz]. Lechitic and Slovak turned the Proto-Slavic palatalized stop *ď [dʲ] into dz: *meďa 'border' > Polish miedza, Slovak medza; *saďa 'soot' > Polish, Slovak sadza; *pręďa 'yarn' > Polish przędza, Slovak priadza. Belarusian dzekanne turns soft /dʲ/ into a (palatalized) affricate [dzʲ]: дзень 'day', дзед 'grandfather' (cf. Russian день [dʲenʲ], дед [dʲet]).",
  "phoneticEffects": "Affrication, Assibilation",
